WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.404
Hello . . . Who are you?

2
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:14.054
I'm a Nile crocodile.

3
00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:18.178
We're the biggest reptiles on earth.

4
00:00:18.179 --> 00:00:21.025
Where do you live?

5
00:00:21.026 --> 00:00:25.199
Nile crocodiles live mostly in Africa.

6
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.400
We like warm swamps, rivers, and marshes.

7
00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:33.372
Your teeth look sharp!

8
00:00:33.373 --> 00:00:40.050
We have more than sixty teeth.

9
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:43.265
But we can't chew with them.

10
00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:48.275
We can only bite.

11
00:00:48.276 --> 00:00:50.789
What do you eat?

12
00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.050
We eat fish, turtles, and crabs.

13
00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:58.977
Our strong jaws open very wide.

14
00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:03.611
So we can eat zebras and hippos too.

15
00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:06.678
Are you dangerous?

16
00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:11.817
Yes! Nile crocodiles are very dangerous.

17
00:01:11.818 --> 00:01:16.367
Sometimes we eat people!

18
00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:19.152
Yikes!

19
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:24.556
But Nile crocodiles are very caring parents.

20
00:01:24.557 --> 00:01:29.282
Most reptiles don't stay with their eggs.

21
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:35.366
We protect our eggs fiercely!

22
00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:38.058
How do you swim?

23
00:01:38.059 --> 00:01:42.022
We use our powerful tails to move.

24
00:01:42.023 --> 00:01:46.226
Our eyes and ears stay above the water.

25
00:01:46.227 --> 00:01:51.028
That helps us see and hear.

26
00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:54.094
I'm ready for a swim now.

27
00:01:54.095 --> 00:01:56.372
Bye!

28
00:01:56.373 --> 00:02:05.639
Good-bye, Nile Crocodile.

